> API and interpretation

Words use signed1-based generator IDs; zero, invalid IDs and INT_MIN magnitudes
outside range reject before table allocation. Total definitions differ from live
rows after coincidences. Complete word, actual table and selected-operation
policies are separate. Closed compact actions are independently checked against
inverse columns and every relation; unresolved partial tables never claim a
finite group certificate.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

> References

- Todd and Coxeter, A Practical Method for Enumerating Cosets of a Finite
  Abstract Group, Proceedings of the Edinburgh Mathematical Society5
  (1936),26-34

